                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Played on Steam Deck.\r\n\r\nI should have checked my negative review for Skipper 1 before buying the cheap sale for this sequel. At least this one has music, which is something I noted was missing from the first game, and it's rather nice here. Also I liked the gag of having some story text for the first 13 levels just to fourth wall break and drop it, that was funny.\r\n\r\nAchievements are broken in this game, like they were in the first one. The first 21 levels are boringly easy, but then 22 is an unexpected difficulty spike and then 23-25 are good. Again the credits say \"More puzzles will be out soon\" but the first game said that and had nothing for five years just to add the three puzzles from the demo.",
